WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
Friday, February 12th

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.830
We will be starting soon

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:11.800
<i>Action!</i>

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:19.810
<i>Hey there! To all the first timers,
nice to meet you.</i>

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:22.190
<i>For everyone else, it's been a week!
Long time no see!</i>

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:23.600
<i>I'm your streamer, Myu!</i>

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:27.400
<i>Thank you for watching "Myu's Nicco Nico
Live Fortune Telling" again today!</i>

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.110
<i>I'm super happy!</i>

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:32.570
<i>Since you took your time to drop by,
please enjoy the show!</i>

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:36.120
LICK LICK LICK LICK

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.490
<i>Just because you're puppies
doesn't mean you can lick so much!</i>

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:42.710
<i>Anyways, this show is where I, Myu,
a self-proclaimed fortune teller,</i>

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:44.960
<i>openly tells fortunes of others
on live stream.</i>

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:49.800
<i>I take the liberty of calling all of you
"distressed puppies" on the show,</i>

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:51.840
Waiting for distressed puppies seeking counsel!

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:51.840
Myu's Nicco Nico Live Fortune Telling

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:50.960
<i>so please take heed of that.</i>

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:52.880
<i>Anyways, are we all ready?</i>

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.840
<i>This is Myu's number.</i>

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.100
Now then, let's be eager here.
Who's the first distressed puppy for today?

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:58.470
Private Number

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:02.140
All right, I've decided!

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:03.640
And a push!

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:05.150
Hello? Hi there!

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:06.560
Please tell me your name.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:11.860
<i>I-It doesn't matter
what my name is, right?</i>

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:14.700
<i>How much are you getting paid
from the site admins?</i>

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:16.410
Wh-What?

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:18.030
<i>You're getting paid money, right?</i>

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:19.530
<i>No, you're paying them, aren't you?</i>

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:22.540
<i>Everyone who's sought advice until now
are all f-fakes, aren't they?</i>

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:22.540
<i>Hang up!</i>

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:24.620
Well then...

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:26.580
<i>About me 10 years from now...</i>

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.380
<i>Give me my fortune
for how I'm doing ten years from now.</i>

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:31.670
Ten years from now...

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:34.130
<i>Right. Ten years from now.
How I've ended up.</i>

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.550
<i>I'm scared.</i>

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:43.560
<i>Okay! Let's fortune-tell
what you'll be like ten years from now!</i>

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:45.640
<i>I'm scared to tell fortunes.</i>

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:46.980
<i>"Let's fortune-tell," huh?</i>

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:48.480
<i>But I have to keep going.</i>

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:49.770
<i>Now you've said it.</i>

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.520
<i>That's what I must continue to do.</i>

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:55.200
Open, Keter!

00:01:57.610 --> 00:01:59.870
A 2026 calendar.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.410
A beautiful office.

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:04.700
It seems like you're using
a computer to do some work.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:08.710
It's not a laptop or anything
but a much bigger computer...

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:18.430
<i>This is absolutely terrible!
Now it's been proven that you're bogus.</i>

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:20.180
<i>You totally are bogus!</i>

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:22.470
<i>That's not even close to the level
of a fortune-telling, you skank!</i>

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:24.100
It's not bogus!
I did see a proper vision!

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:27.230
<i>Oh, I forgot to tell you, but I've got
terminal cancer with one year left to live.</i>

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.520
<i>And you saw something
ten years in the future for such a guy?</i>

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.190
<i>Of course not, you piece of crap!</i>

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:33.270
So you were going to deceive me
from the beginning?

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:35.570
Can you prove that you only
have one year left to live?

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:37.650
<i>What? You want to come
meet me right now?</i>

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:39.280
<i>I'll show you my medical report.</i>

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.030
<i>And I'm so electrohypersensitive
that I'm limited by the doctors.</i>

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.950
<i>Do you know
what electrohypersensitivity is?</i>

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:48.420
<i>If you don't know,
google it, you damn skank!</i>

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.090
<i>Daddy...</i>

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:54.630
<i>Hey, how do you feel right now?</i>

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.970
<i>How do you feel now that someone
saw through your bogus ways?</i>

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:58.840
<i>Help me, Papa...</i>

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.720
<i>Was I wrong after all...</i>

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:03.390
<i>...Papa?</i>

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:35.020
Monday, February 22nd

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:40.860
Moritsuka!

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:43.240
What was it like at the scene?

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:47.160
Division One over at headquarters
kicked me out midway.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:49.290
Tell us what the situation is like.

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:52.080
The victim is Isayuki Hashigami,
51 years old.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:54.540
Professor at Seimei University
School of Science and Engineering.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:56.500
The scene is Professor Hashigami's
laboratory.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:58.460
Sixth floor of building 10 over there.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:02.130
Estimated time of death
is between 5 pm and 7 pm today.

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:05.550
Well, we don't know
the cause of death yet.

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:07.300
You don't need that "well."

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.760
Oh, excuse me.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:10.850
What do you mean,
you don't know which?

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:12.480
Is that what the forensic experts
are saying?

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:14.560
Apparently there were
countless exterior wounds.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.690
Maybe he was tortured or something.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:18.820
Apparently, his legs were tied up.

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:21.820
The victim's trademark long hair
was all ripped out, as well.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:23.700
Oh, that's right.

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:26.450
There was one bloodstained knife
left at the scene.

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:29.280
It was as if it was screaming,
"This is the murder weapon!"

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:30.370
And any prints?

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:32.290
Apparently there are some prints on it.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.120
Please ask the forensic experts
for details.

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:36.960
Oh, and one more thing.

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:38.750
What? Don't put on airs like that.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:41.090
The victim's tooth...

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:44.470
No way... I don't believe this!

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:51.180
Is that what you'd call a dying message?

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:53.430
<i>Hey, you there! You stupid face there!</i>

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:56.440
<i>What are you panicking for?
Get a grip, you idiot!</i>

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:57.980
Wh-Who is it? Where are you?

00:05:57.480 --> 00:05:58.400
<i>Calm down!</i>

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.270
I didn't do anything!

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:07.320
<i>Jeez!</i>

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:09.740
<i>You don't have time to cry, you idiot!
Look at your bag!</i>

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:14.080
<i>How long do you plan on staying there?</i>

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:17.000
<i>Do you realize that at this rate,
you're sure to become one of the suspects?</i>

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.500
What's this?
Which station's show is it—

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:19.790
<i>It's not a TV show!</i>

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:23.170
<i>Hey, I'm talking to you right there!</i>

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:26.380
<i>Nose dripping, to sink to the floor
in front of a corpse and fretting about...</i>

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:27.380
<i>I mean you!</i>

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:29.090
Who are you?

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:31.810
Wait, why are voices coming
out of this thing? It's not normal at all!

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:34.770
<i>You are about to be roped
into a very dangerous case.</i>

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:36.180
Did you frame me into a trap?
Why are you doing—

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:36.180
<i>Shut up!</i>

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:38.980
<i>This is partly due to your
thoughtless actions, as well!</i>

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:40.730
<i>It's not that
you're about to be roped into it...</i>

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:42.860
<i>You're here to become roped into it
because you want to!</i>

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:47.990
Don't yell at me,
and give me a proper explanation!

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:49.070
<i>We don't have time for that!</i>

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:52.330
<i>Anyway, I'm going to tell you something
important right now, so listen up.</i>

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:55.620
<i>If you want to escape from there,
obey the directions we give you. Got that?</i>

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.370
<i>Do you see that there's a toolbox
underneath the desk?</i>

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:01.210
D-Did you put it there?

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.210
<i>Pull out a pair of pliers from it!</i>

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:04.250
<i>Hurry!</i>

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:06.630
Pliers? For what?

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:08.090
I don't have to break
the lock on the door to—

00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:09.800
<i>That's not it! You're going to pull out
the professor's tooth!</i>

00:07:10.010 --> 00:07:10.890
A tooth?

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:11.930
<i>You're going to pull out his tooth!</i>

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:13.390
Y-You've got to be kidding me!

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:16.220
There's no way doing something like that
will let me get away from here!

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:18.270
<i>You're going to pull
the left most tooth on the bottom!</i>

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:19.690
<i>You can't make a mistake there, okay?</i>

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:20.690
Listen to me!

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:22.900
<i>Do you still not realize the situation
you've put yourself into right now?</i>

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:25.860
<i>You've already touched
one of the murder weapons already!</i>

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:28.320
I... I'm such an idiot!

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:30.450
<i>Stop dillydallying!
People will show up soon!</i>

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:33.200
But... But... Pulling out a tooth...
Something like that...

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:35.620
Something like that is impossible.

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:37.790
<i>Just hurry up and do it!
You don't have time left!</i>

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.660
I don't have time? Just how much—

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:40.580
<i>30 more seconds!</i>

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:42.380
Th-Thirty seconds?

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:43.130
<i>Hurry!</i>

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:44.040
Dammit!

00:07:46.670 --> 00:07:49.590
<i>He's got a gold tooth in the back
on the left side. Pull just that one out!</i>

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:50.800
<i>20 more seconds!</i>

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:51.630
<i>Hurry!</i>

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:53.220
I know that!

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:55.390
<i>10 more seconds!</i>

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:59.520
Come out!

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:56.970
<i>Five seconds!</i>

00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:06.820
<i>They're here.</i>

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:23.330
Hey...

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:24.460
Hey!

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:28.170
What's with this...

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:31.130
That's right, the gold tooth...

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:35.970
You're kidding me. Can this really be...

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:37.720
This is a key, right?

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:40.480
When was the victim's tooth pulled?

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:43.480
At the least, you can say
for certain it was today.

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:46.480
That's right, there was
one more suspicious thing.

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:50.360
This is purely from a personal investigation
that I, Shun Moritsuka, did,

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:52.320
but there's a certain
doujin manga out there.

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:54.320
What's that doujin manga thing?

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.320
Shinoyama-senpai, you don't know?

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:57.700
You're so behind the times!

00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:01.200
Doujin is what you'd classify
as "indies" for music.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:03.210
Manga has nothing to do
with this right now.

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:04.960
Or so you think!

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:08.590
But on the contrary, there is,
though nobody realizes it right now.

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:11.670
When I heard about this case,
it immediately dawned on me.

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:13.630
I guess it was something
characteristic for otakus.

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:16.510
So was there a copy
of this doujin manga at the scene?

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:19.350
No, that's not it. I'm talking about this.

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:21.850
It's an adult doujin targeted at women.

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:24.480
The author is a woman
named Ririka Nishizono.

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:30.650
A scene in this book has a striking
resemblance to the crime details for this case.

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:32.820
After a man stabs another man,

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:35.700
he takes the dead man's tooth
with a knife as a memento

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:37.620
and lovingly takes it with him...

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:38.910
- Moritsuka...
- Yes?

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:41.080
That really ruined the mood.

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:43.160
Out of the question.

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:44.410
Wait, what?

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:47.460
Jeez!

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:51.500
I gave them information
equivalent to a huge scoop, too!

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:56.470
Weren't they taught as kids to listen
to someone's story until the very end?

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:01.310
Agent Moritsuka.

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:03.140
<i>Japanese is fine.</i>

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:05.390
Agent Moritsuka here.

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:07.310
<i>Is this line safe?</i>

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:11.190
Don't underestimate an otaku.
This is a perfectly scrambled signal.

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:14.740
It would be impossible for anyone
to analyze this perfect algorithm.

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:16.150
<i>What's the situation?</i>

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:19.870
The rain is so depressing.
I wish I made a sunny-weather doll.

00:10:20.410 --> 00:10:22.870
<i>According to forecasts,
the rain will stop by tomorrow afternoon.</i>

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:24.870
You're an honest man.

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:26.500
<i>Were you able to get the list?</i>

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:27.500
No.

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:30.920
I didn't find the actual list,
but there were some fruits for my labor.

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:36.510
The list we've been after may not exist
in this world in the first place.

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:38.050
<i>What do you mean?</i>

00:10:38.050 --> 00:10:38.970
It's a "CODE."

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:42.010
He was polite enough
to write that down as his dying message.

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:42.850
<i>That's not good.</i>

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:44.390
Of course, there are no problems with it.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:46.730
I erased it before they figured it out.

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:49.770
Sheesh, it was a good thing
I was at the crime scene first!

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:54.780
They don't realize that the list
they want to get rid of has been encoded.

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:56.700
<i>So you mean the list exists?</i>

00:10:57.030 --> 00:11:01.410
Yeah, but they took the effort
to encode it to camouflage.

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:04.200
I'd venture to think
there aren't any paperwork left of it.

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:06.540
I don't think the professor is that stupid.

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:08.870
<i>We don't have time. Find the list.</i>

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:12.670
Time? Do you mean
the time limit of life?

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:16.420
In any case,
there are too many guinea pigs.

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:19.050
All 256 of them...

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:22.510
But in the end...

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:25.600
you probably won't be
able to change the future.

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:29.270
Friday, February 19th

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:30.480
<i>Yes, hello!</i>

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:32.310
<i>This is Nicco Nico Live Fortune Telling!</i>

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:34.650
<i>Welcome, distressed puppy.</i>

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:36.110
<i>Please give me your name.</i>

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:38.320
I'm SARAI.

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:39.070
SARAI is here!

00:11:39.070 --> 00:11:39.700
Some kind of celebrity??

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:41.450
Myu, ruuuuun!

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:41.450
<i>So you're SARAI, nice to meet—</i>

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:45.080
Why isn't fortune telling on the streets
profitable? Do you know why, Myu?

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:51.580
<i>It's difficult for most fortune tellers
to earn a living with just fortune telling.</i>

00:11:51.830 --> 00:11:54.840
<i>I've done personal research
with about ten fortune tellers.</i>

00:11:55.090 --> 00:11:59.220
<i>Every one of them said
they had a job other than fortune telling.</i>

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:00.380
<i>Do you understand the meaning of this?</i>

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:02.090
H-Huh? What are you talking—

00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:04.970
Why can't fortune tellers make a living
with just fortune telling?

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:07.270
If necessary, they can see
their own futures

00:12:07.270 --> 00:12:11.230
and choose the paths that allow them
to succeed as fortune tellers.

00:12:11.690 --> 00:12:13.230
But the reason they don't do that

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:14.400
Shut up, you piece of crap.

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:16.020
is because they can't see
the future by fortune telling.

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:16.360
Thanks for your personal note,
thanks for this farce.

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:19.360
Yes, that's right, this is a farce.

00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:22.490
But what you're doing
is a farce, as well, Myu.

00:12:22.780 --> 00:12:27.450
<i>Those that believe that this is fortune-telling
should reconsider it right away.</i>

00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:34.210
It's fine.

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:39.760
I'm sure... I'm sure that despite everything,
SARAI is a distressed puppy, too.

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:43.510
<i>I... I'm not in distress at all.</i>

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:48.100
Open, Yesod!

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:51.180
<i>Why do you have to be murdered?</i>

00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:52.600
<i>Who in the world would do such a thing?</i>

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:54.230
<i>I had so many things
I wanted to tell you!</i>

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:56.360
<i>How many months
have I not spoken with you?</i>

00:12:56.770 --> 00:12:59.280
<i>Why did I despise you so much as I did?</i>

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:01.740
<i>Hey, say something...</i>

00:13:02.530 --> 00:13:03.150
Dad.

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:08.950
<i>Hurry!</i>

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:10.370
<i>Please, SARAI!</i>

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:12.330
<i>You should hurry
and speak with your father!</i>

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:14.370
Why are you suddenly talking about Dad?

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:18.880
If you want to start over with your father,
listen to his story well!

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:22.050
<i>There are things you want to speak
with your father about, right?</i>

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:23.130
<i>Now is the only time!</i>

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:25.590
If you put it off, you'll totally regret it!

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:28.760
<i>S-Such a list of words that come
from a template! Completely meaningless!</i>

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:29.890
Or are you threatening me?

00:13:30.100 --> 00:13:32.640
<i>You think that by hinting suggestively
at the death of relatives,</i>

00:13:32.810 --> 00:13:35.020
you can assume mental dominance!

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:37.230
<i>I will not succumb to intimidation!</i>

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:41.030
<i>I don't have...</i>

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:45.740
the power to change destiny!

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:50.620
You need to move on your own!

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:52.870
<i>The card means...</i>

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:56.880
"turn everything to void
and look over oneself."

00:13:56.880 --> 00:13:57.880
<i>Yeah?</i>

00:13:57.880 --> 00:13:58.380
Tuesday, February 23rd

00:13:58.840 --> 00:14:01.420
So SARAI called in just that one time?

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:03.260
Yes, that was it.

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:07.390
There's no mistake about that story
about SARAI and his father?

00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:11.140
Oh, yes. That was what I heard,
in his voice.

00:14:12.020 --> 00:14:13.930
Um... Did something happen?

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:16.810
You came all the way out
to do a questioning, which surprised me.

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:18.150
Yes, a bit.

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:21.360
I'm investigating into all connections
with SARAI that I know of.

00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:22.730
I see...

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:24.650
By the way, about your abilities...

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:28.410
Is there anyone else that knows
about it, or you spoke about it to?

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:29.910
Who among those close to you?

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:31.870
Well...

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:33.370
that would be...

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:35.790
Yes. I did an interview
with her in the past,

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:37.370
and I've known her since.

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:40.920
And you believe
in Miyuu Aikawa's fortune telling?

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:42.960
I believe the fact
that she gets many views

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:46.720
is because she's gaining popularity
as her fortunes are hitting spot-on.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:48.840
That can't be the only reason, I think.

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:51.100
There could just be people
who are pleasure-seekers.

00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:54.430
I think that may not
necessarily be the case.

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:56.690
Do you have some
logical reasoning behind it?

00:14:56.940 --> 00:15:02.400
Spiritually speaking, speed of time is faster
for the mental than the physical.

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:06.610
Therefore, if you can tack on your
consciousness onto the mental side...

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:09.820
I believe you can speed time up
or rewind it.

00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:13.280
Though, all of this is merely a copy
of what Mr. Hashigami said.

00:15:13.790 --> 00:15:16.500
It sounds like you believe
in Professor Hashigami

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:18.540
more than you believe
in Miyuu Aikawa.

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:21.330
It was such a shame for Mr. Hashigami.

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:23.170
He was a very good man.

00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:26.050
According to Professor Hashigami's logic,

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:28.840
the consciousness can head
toward the past, as well, right?

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:29.840
That's how it would be.

00:15:30.090 --> 00:15:31.800
The opposite of what happened to Miyuu.

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:34.260
This is a case of the mental side
that resided in the past,

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:36.640
staying there and affecting humans
in the present.

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:38.730
Ria Minase...

00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:40.900
The high school girl
that lived with a mummy...

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:42.810
Do you remember her at all?

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:46.650
Ria Minase...

00:15:46.990 --> 00:15:49.030
Oh, I remember her, I remember her!

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:56.410
A little sister who lived with her
rotten big brother for a year

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:56.410
So bizarre!
A mummy found in Kichijoji!

00:15:49.450 --> 00:15:51.360
Ria Minase.
That's the name of the little sister.

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:54.030
I thought her name sounded
like a TV personality.

00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:57.200
She took the corpse of her elder brother
from the hospital three years ago

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:58.790
after he died from medical malpractice,

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:00.670
and apparently lived together
with it for a year.

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:03.540
I believe it was determined that
the chances of an incident was low,

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:06.050
and she lives normally now.

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:09.260
Her Fadebook entries
aren't all too normal.

00:16:09.630 --> 00:16:10.470
Take a look.

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:11.930
This is...

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:15.680
Something's wrong...
What's wrong with Gamota?

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:17.930
That boy now showing up
this late in the day...

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:19.850
Is there going to be
an earthquake soon?

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:23.980
It may be due to black magic
that's more terrifying than an earthquake!

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:26.570
What, did you curse him or something?

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:30.320
Well, you see, back when we went
to the Kurenaino Mansion for an interview...

00:16:30.570 --> 00:16:32.110
<i>What is your request?</i>

00:16:32.110 --> 00:16:34.950
<i>I want you to punish my senpai
for two-timing on me!</i>

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:36.830
<i>Two-timing...
Who is the other woman involved?</i>

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:38.240
<i>It was...</i>

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:39.000
<i>her!</i>

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:41.920
<i>I'm sorry for making
a request like this...</i>

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:44.790
<i>It seems you have
a rather complicated situation.</i>

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:48.460
<i>Please write down information about
the person you want to put a curse on.</i>

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:49.420
<i>Okay!</i>

00:16:49.420 --> 00:16:51.380
<i>I'm sorry,
but I'd like to know how much...</i>

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:53.970
<i>We have three courses ready for you.</i>

00:16:54.220 --> 00:16:58.930
<i>The lowest rank is the "Tomorrow's Despair"
course at 9,990 yen.</i>

00:16:58.930 --> 00:17:00.350
<i>I'll be using one doll.</i>

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:04.810
<i>The middle rank is "Deathrattle Scream"
at 42,420 yen.</i>

00:17:05.110 --> 00:17:09.280
<i>The highest ranking course
is the "Demon's Ritual" at 66,600 yen.</i>

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:12.320
<i>It goes without saying,
we'd like the best one!</i>

00:17:12.570 --> 00:17:14.490
<i>You can pay for it at the very end.</i>

00:17:14.740 --> 00:17:15.910
<i>Okay!</i>

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:18.370
Wait up, didn't you go a bit too far?

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:21.450
That totally worked! Ishishu!

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:23.750
I hope Gamo-senpai is all right.

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:26.750
<i>That girl Aria's powers were for real.</i>

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:29.090
<i>Why does she act as an agent for curses?</i>

00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:32.590
<i>Maybe she has a hidden reason, like I do.</i>

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:38.760
<i>March 20th.</i>

00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:43.020
<i>Big Brother took me out
for a drive in his new car.</i>

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:48.150
<i>But Big Brother just got his license,
so his driving wasn't all that good.</i>

00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:50.730
<i>He's bad with directions,
so he took the wrong turn many times,</i>

00:17:50.730 --> 00:17:53.530
<i>and we were unable to reach
the Shonan beach.</i>

00:17:53.860 --> 00:17:59.830
<i>But Big Brother, I was very happy
just sitting right next to you.</i>

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:02.580
<i>Going out for a drive
for hours on end together with you...</i>

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:04.710
<i>That alone almost put tears in my eyes.</i>

00:18:04.710 --> 00:18:06.290
<i>Please take me out again sometime.</i>

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:09.420
Talk about some ridiculous
attachment to your brother...

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:11.300
Just keep reading the posts after this.

00:18:12.010 --> 00:18:13.340
<i>May 12th.</i>

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:16.300
<i>Let's go together to the sea
that you love so much, Big Brother.</i>

00:18:16.590 --> 00:18:18.260
<i>May 13th.</i>

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:22.180
<i>Big Brother coaxed me
into making him some French toast.</i>

00:18:22.680 --> 00:18:24.060
<i>May 14th.</i>

00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:26.810
<i>Let's go together to the sea
that you love so much, Big Brother.</i>

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:28.560
<i>May 15th.</i>

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:31.570
<i>There is a terrible smell...
I took many showers.</i>

00:18:32.230 --> 00:18:33.690
<i>May 17th.</i>

00:18:33.690 --> 00:18:36.700
<i>Let's go together to the sea
that you love so much, Big Brother.</i>

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:38.910
<i>May 21st.</i>

00:18:39.410 --> 00:18:40.580
<i>So many bugs.</i>

00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:44.410
STOP STOP STOP STOP STOP

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:42.740
<i>May 22nd.</i>

00:18:42.740 --> 00:18:46.080
<i>Let's go together to the sea
that you love so much, Big Brother.</i>

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:49.330
Such a terrible way
to get attached to your brother!

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:52.210
If that really was the case,
it would be a laughing matter.

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:56.880
But by this date, May 12th,
her big brother had already passed away.

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:57.970
Sumikaze...

00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:01.470
That would be where most detectives'
moods would be ruined,

00:19:01.470 --> 00:19:03.770
but that catches my interest even more!

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:05.390
That's a relief to hear.

00:19:05.640 --> 00:19:09.400
This is my theory, though it's also
secondhand from Mr. Hashigami...

00:19:09.650 --> 00:19:12.980
Perhaps this girl was living together
with her big brother's ghost.

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:14.570
<i>Concerning the case where yesterday,</i>

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:15.990
MUSASHINO
UNIVERSITY PROFESSOR MURDERED

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:17.240
<i>around 11 pm, within the campus of
Seimei University in Musashino City, Tokyo...</i>

00:19:17.240 --> 00:19:18.820
<i>Isayuki Hashigami,</i>

00:19:18.820 --> 00:19:21.910
<i>professor in the university's Science and
Engineering department, was murdered...</i>

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:20.490
So you are here.

00:19:21.030 --> 00:19:21.910
Yeah.

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:23.620
Is this your doing?

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:26.160
Do you think I killed him?

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:29.870
We decided that you will not kill those
we put curses on during the pact—

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:36.090
In his case, I didn't put my hands
on him just yet.

00:19:36.090 --> 00:19:37.880
I thought it would be okay to do so,

00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:40.760
but someone else killed him
before I got to him.

00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:43.010
This case is definitely a bit fishy.

00:19:43.010 --> 00:19:45.680
If there are guys out there
that want to lure me into a trap,

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:47.310
I have to come up with new plans.

00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:49.640
I'm gonna have you help me.

00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:53.940
If you refuse, the next head
that will blow will be yours. Got that?

00:19:53.940 --> 00:19:54.440
Thursday, February 25th

00:19:55.610 --> 00:19:59.030
That senpai is really suspicious!
You shouldn't deal with him at all!

00:19:59.570 --> 00:20:02.530
Gamo-senpai is a weird guy,
but he's not suspicious.

00:20:02.530 --> 00:20:06.750
You think so? I mean, he's running
some really sketchy website, right?

00:20:06.750 --> 00:20:10.460
I saw it. He was writing
a comical article about you too, Myu.

00:20:10.460 --> 00:20:13.000
Myu? Chi, you read that?

00:20:15.170 --> 00:20:16.210
Chi?

00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:18.800
Myu, are you really all right?

00:20:18.800 --> 00:20:22.220
You really do slack a bit in places...
so it makes me worry.

00:20:22.220 --> 00:20:26.350
Slack? Nobody other than you
has said that to me, Chi.

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:30.850
If you think it's even a bit risky,
you can contact me at any time.

00:20:37.400 --> 00:20:40.820
I'm so happy
I can be friends with you, Chi!

00:20:41.070 --> 00:20:42.200
There, there.

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:46.580
As your guardian, I'll diligently
take care of the slacking Myu.

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:51.210
Then, buy me a whipped cream
chocolate banana crepe at Circus next time!

00:20:51.210 --> 00:20:52.460
Don't get carried away!

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:56.290
CHUO LINE - KICHIJOJI STATION

00:20:56.590 --> 00:20:59.510
Well, I'm going to stop
by that pet shop over there.

00:20:59.510 --> 00:21:01.010
Chi, you're going to raise a pet?

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:04.640
A parakeet. You know, Myu, you saw
my fortune the other day, right?

00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:08.140
Oh, when I looked over you,
Chi, I saw a little bird.

00:21:08.140 --> 00:21:09.930
It's been on my mind ever since,

00:21:09.930 --> 00:21:12.980
and when I saw pictures of birds online,
I got an urge to raise one.

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:16.110
Wow, that's so nice!
But, Chi, you're terrible at taking pictures.

00:21:16.110 --> 00:21:17.690
Don't say that!

00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:20.280
I can't afford it with just my allowance,

00:21:20.740 --> 00:21:22.740
so I'm asking Mom for a favor right now.

00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:24.320
It would be nice if you can convince her.

00:21:24.320 --> 00:21:27.330
Yeah. Until then, I'm just going to
spend time with it at the shop.

00:21:27.700 --> 00:21:28.870
See you later!

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:29.870
Later!

00:21:30.370 --> 00:21:31.540
Bye-bye!

00:21:42.170 --> 00:21:43.170
I'm home!

00:21:49.220 --> 00:21:51.390
Chi, your photo is a bit blurry again.

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:54.640
Got it!

00:21:54.640 --> 00:21:56.600
The little bird

00:21:54.810 --> 00:21:56.100
A ghost photograph?

00:21:58.110 --> 00:21:59.320
What is this?

00:22:06.450 --> 00:22:10.240
<i>The number you have dialed is either
in a location that receives no reception</i>

00:22:10.240 --> 00:22:13.500
<i>or is turned off and unable to answer.</i>

00:22:13.710 --> 00:22:15.000
Chi?

00:23:51.850 --> 00:23:52.600
This program is a work of fiction.
Any resemblance to people, parties,
or situations is purely coincidental.
